    "passageId": "psat-mock-10-passage-010",
    "prompt": "Acousticians compare small performance spaces and find that audiences do not judge clarity from reverberation time alone. Wall geometry and listener position also affect perceived clarity, so a single measured property cannot explain every judgment. The later evidence makes a previously plausible interpretation less complete. The word is chosen because the surrounding discussion requires a precise description of scope or effect. In context, the word identifies a relationship between the observation and its consequence. The surrounding sentence shows that the term refers to a relationship, not merely to a surface feature.\n\nIn this context, the word “derive” most nearly means which of the following?",
    "choices": [
      "make the claim apply equally in every possible setting",
      "obtain from a particular source or process",
      "remove the distinction between the two conditions",
      "make the reported result disappear entirely"
    ],
    "answer": "B",
    "explanation": "In context, “derive” is used with the meaning represented by the keyed choice.",
