    "passageId": "psat-mock-02-passage-104",
    "prompt": "Acousticians compare small performance spaces and find that audiences do not judge clarity from reverberation time alone. Wall geometry and listener position also affect perceived clarity, so a single measured property cannot explain every judgment. The later evidence makes a previously plausible interpretation less complete. The author uses the term to describe the effect while preserving the passage’s limiting condition. The author uses the word to specify the scope or direction of the reported effect. The context contrasts the relevant effect with a different possible interpretation.\n\nIn this context, the word “yield” most nearly means which of the following?",
    "choices": [
      "make the claim apply equally in every possible setting",
      "remove the distinction between the two conditions",
      "make the reported result disappear entirely",
      "produce or result in"
    ],
