    "referenceSheetRelevant": false,
    "passageId": "psat-mock-03-passage-001",
    "prompt": "Leena considers a faded theater sign an eyesore until she learns that volunteers repaint its lettering after renovations. The sign then becomes evidence of repeated community involvement rather than simply an aging facade. The second observation narrows the conclusion that could reasonably be drawn from the first. The context uses the word to mark a relationship rather than simply name a topic or feature. Here, the word characterizes how the evidence affects the interpretation. The surrounding evidence makes the meaning depend on the condition described in the passage.\n\nIn this context, the word “distinguish” most nearly means which of the following?",
    "choices": [
      "show a meaningful difference between",
      "describe a cause that the passage never identifies",
      "refer only to the author’s personal reaction to the topic",
      "repeat the earlier observation without changing its meaning"
    ],
    "answer": "A",
    "explanation": "In context, “distinguish” is used with the meaning represented by the keyed choice.",
