    "prompt": "A city staggers market deliveries to reduce congestion on its busiest streets. Traffic falls there, while smaller side streets experience a different pattern because some deliveries have shifted rather than disappeared. The second observation narrows the conclusion that could reasonably be drawn from the first. The word is chosen because the surrounding discussion requires a precise description of scope or effect. In this passage, the word refers to the way one condition shapes the result. The author uses the term to connect the immediate observation with its larger implication.\n\nIn this context, the word “derive” most nearly means which of the following?",
