    "prompt": "Acousticians compare small performance spaces and find that audiences do not judge clarity from reverberation time alone. Wall geometry and listener position also affect perceived clarity, so a single measured property cannot explain every judgment. The later evidence makes a previously plausible interpretation less complete. The term helps the passage separate the reported pattern from an explanation that would be too broad. The word is used to characterize what happens when the relevant condition changes. The context contrasts the relevant effect with a different possible interpretation.\n\nIn this context, the word “register” most nearly means which of the following?",
