    "prompt": "Engineers test whether a coating changes battery-electrode stability during repeated charge cycles. Coated electrodes retain capacity more consistently, although the benefit becomes smaller at the highest cycling temperature. The second observation narrows the conclusion that could reasonably be drawn from the first. The term appears where the author connects a specific observation to the condition that shapes it. The author uses the word to specify the scope or direction of the reported effect. The term contributes to a qualification that keeps the author’s conclusion appropriately narrow.\n\nIn this context, the word “fracture” most nearly means which of the following?",
