    "passageId": "psat-mock-05-passage-015",
    "prompt": "A linguist compares two related dialects and finds several expressions used before uncertain claims. The expressions vary with audience and setting, indicating that uncertainty is communicated through more than one grammatical feature. The contrast between the two observations reveals why the initial evidence alone is insufficient. The surrounding language gives the word a meaning tied to the passage’s specific pattern of evidence. The author uses the word to describe the practical effect of the change. The term contributes to a qualification that keeps the author’s conclusion appropriately narrow.\n\nIn this context, the word “acknowledge” most nearly means which of the following?",
