    "prompt": "Acousticians compare small performance spaces and find that audiences do not judge clarity from reverberation time alone. Wall geometry and listener position also affect perceived clarity, so a single measured property cannot explain every judgment. The later evidence makes a previously plausible interpretation less complete. The word is chosen because the surrounding discussion requires a precise description of scope or effect. The author uses the word to describe the practical effect of the change. The term helps distinguish the observed result from a broader conclusion the passage does not establish.\n\nIn this context, the word “trace” most nearly means which of the following?",
