    "prompt": "A gardener removes a broken gate expecting the courtyard to become easier to maintain. Neighbors begin crossing the open space and lingering there, so a maintenance decision unexpectedly changes how the courtyard is used. The later evidence makes a previously plausible interpretation less complete. The term helps the author distinguish what the evidence shows from what it merely might suggest. The surrounding discussion uses the word to distinguish the observed result from a broader claim. The term helps distinguish the observed result from a broader conclusion the passage does not establish.\n\nIn this context, the word “illuminate” most nearly means which of the following?",
