    "prompt": "Acousticians compare small performance spaces and find that audiences do not judge clarity from reverberation time alone. Wall geometry and listener position also affect perceived clarity, so a single measured property cannot explain every judgment. The later evidence makes a previously plausible interpretation less complete. The wording places the term between the observation and the conclusion the author draws from it. The author uses the word to describe the practical effect of the change. The context contrasts the relevant effect with a different possible interpretation.\n\nIn this context, the word “encounter” most nearly means which of the following?",
