    "prompt": "Acousticians compare small performance spaces and find that audiences do not judge clarity from reverberation time alone. Wall geometry and listener position also affect perceived clarity, so a single measured property cannot explain every judgment. The later evidence makes a previously plausible interpretation less complete. The word is chosen because the surrounding discussion requires a precise description of scope or effect. In this passage, the word refers to the way one condition shapes the result. The context contrasts the relevant effect with a different possible interpretation.\n\nIn this context, the word “derive” most nearly means which of the following?",
