    "prompt": "Leena considers a faded theater sign an eyesore until she learns that volunteers repaint its lettering after renovations. The sign then becomes evidence of repeated community involvement rather than simply an aging facade. The second observation narrows the conclusion that could reasonably be drawn from the first. Here, the wording makes the effect more precise by limiting what the surrounding evidence establishes. Here, the word describes the role of the feature in the author’s explanation. The surrounding evidence makes the meaning depend on the condition described in the passage.\n\nIn this context, the word “underscore” most nearly means which of the following?",
