    "passageId": "sat-mock-02-passage-074",
    "prompt": "Engineers test whether a coating changes battery-electrode stability during repeated charge cycles. Coated electrodes retain capacity more consistently, although the benefit becomes smaller at the highest cycling temperature. The second observation narrows the conclusion that could reasonably be drawn from the first. The author selects the term to describe how one part of the evidence changes the significance of another. In this passage, the word refers to the way one condition shapes the result. The author uses the term to connect the immediate observation with its larger implication.\n\nIn this context, the word “unsettle” most nearly means which of the following?",
