    "prompt": "Engineers test whether a coating changes battery-electrode stability during repeated charge cycles. Coated electrodes retain capacity more consistently, although the benefit becomes smaller at the highest cycling temperature. The second observation narrows the conclusion that could reasonably be drawn from the first. Here, the word helps characterize a conditional result rather than an unconditional claim. The author uses the word to describe the practical effect of the change. The author uses the term to connect the immediate observation with its larger implication.\n\nIn this context, the word “reinforce” most nearly means which of the following?",
