    "prompt": "A cooperative changes its purchasing policy after regional prices become less predictable. The change reduces exposure to short-term price swings, but members with different production schedules benefit by different amounts. The contrast between the two observations reveals why the initial evidence alone is insufficient. The term helps the author distinguish what the evidence shows from what it merely might suggest. The author uses the word to specify the scope or direction of the reported effect. The passage uses the term to mark how the evidence should be understood within its limits.\n\nIn this context, the word “illuminate” most nearly means which of the following?",
